{"name":"Argent","hex":"#888888","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Argent","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Argent"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tincture (heraldry)","blocks":[{"text":"Tinctures are the colours, metals, and furs used in heraldry. There are nine tinctures in common use: two metals, five colours, and two furs. The metals are or and argent ; the colours gules (red), azure (blue), vert (green), sable (black), and purpure (purple); and the furs ermine, which is derived from the winter fur of a stoat, and vair, which is derived from the fur of a red squirrel. The use of other tinctures varies depending on the time period and heraldic tradition in question."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/Tinctures_%28metals_and_colours%29.svg/330px-Tinctures_%28metals_and_colours%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tincture_(heraldry)","wikidata":"Q3404720"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Solemn_kanunnik_brugge.jpg/330px-Solemn_kanunnik_brugge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Solemn_kanunnik_brugge.jpg/330px-Solemn_kanunnik_brugge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Canons from the chapter of Bruges, solemn winterdress in fur","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASolemn_kanunnik_brugge.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a1/Kursch.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a1/Kursch.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKursch.